Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840 size patch to user/hamnix/grep.ad (the committed file plus the teensy41 patch's changes, which it repeats).
Applied by scripts/mkroot.sh in build/feather-nrf52840/root only; the
committed file is unchanged.

Reason: the nRF52840 has 256 KiB of RAM for everything: kernel data, kernel
stacks and heap, the files in / and every running program's stack and data
(boards/feather_nrf52840/link.ld; programs' code stays in flash).

    line buffer       64 KiB -> 1 KiB (a longer line is matched in pieces,
                      as Hamnix's grep does past its buffer)
    pattern buffer    8 KiB -> 256 bytes

Only constants, array lengths, and messages that quote them change.
Generated by editing a copy and
    diff -u --label a/user/hamnix/grep.ad --label b/user/hamnix/grep.ad user/hamnix/grep.ad <copy>

--- a/user/hamnix/grep.ad
+++ b/user/hamnix/grep.ad
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@
 f_line:  int32 = 0
 
 # ---- patterns ----
-patbuf:  Array[8192, uint8]
+patbuf:  Array[256, uint8]
 patbuf_len: uint64 = 0
 pat_off: Array[64, int32]
 pat_len: Array[64, int32]
@@ -79,8 +79,8 @@
 active_pat: int32 = -1        # which pattern is currently compiled
 
 # ---- current line + match span ----
-LINE_BUF: uint64 = 65536
-line: Array[65536, uint8]
+LINE_BUF: uint64 = 1024
+line: Array[1024, uint8]
 gm_s: uint64 = 0
 gm_e: uint64 = 0
 
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@
         return
     off: uint64 = patbuf_len
     i: uint64 = 0
-    while s[i] != 0 and patbuf_len < 8192:
+    while s[i] != 0 and patbuf_len < 256:
         patbuf[patbuf_len] = s[i]
         patbuf_len = patbuf_len + 1
         i = i + 1
